  "final_text": "Both the dashboard and the alert rule exist and read back correctly.\n\n**Dashboard: \"EFF-741b78df Web logs overview\"**\n- ID: `eff-741b78df-web-logs-overview-da811d6c50e7`, time range last 7 days, 5 panels:\n  - Total requests (count metric)\n  - Unique client IPs (unique count of `clientip`)\n  - Average response bytes (average of `bytes`)\n  - Requests over time (line, date histogram on `timestamp`)\n  - Requests by response code (bar, top 15 values of `response.keyword`)\n\n**Alert rule: \"EFF-741b78df 5xx spike\"**\n- ID: `30bc0220-348f-4b65-afbe-11fd71c2a3d2`, type `.es-query`, consumer `stackAlerts`, runs every 1m, enabled, tagged `EFF-741b78df`.\n- Index `kibana_sample_data_logs`, time field `timestamp`, 5-minute window, fires when the count is greater than 10.\n- The query filters `response.keyword` lexically from \"500\" to \"599\", which picks out 5xx codes because every code is three digits.\n- It has no action connector, so it records alerts but doesn't notify anyone.\n\n**Choices I made:**\n- I enabled the rule so it runs. The tool creates rules disabled by default, and a disabled rule would not check every minute.\n- I didn't query the data directly. The Kibana endpoints I tried for ES|QL weren't available in this configuration, so I chose the panels and the 5xx filter from the field list rather than from the actual values. I didn't confirm that 5xx responses exist in the sample data, so the rule may never fire.\n- The dashboard's 5xx view is the response-code bar chart. A dedicated 5xx panel would need a filter that the dashboard tool doesn't support.",
